    "text": "\n\n<think>\nHere's a thinking process:\n\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\n   - **Role:** Careful technical writer\n   - **Style:** Plain English, no bullet-only answers, use short paragraphs, then a compact numbered list where clearer\n   - **Topic:** Running a 35B-class MoE model on a phone with 8 GB RAM and UFS flash, comparing three approaches:\n     1. `mmap` the whole file, hope kernel keeps hot pages\n     2. Stream only routed experts per token into an LRU cache (~2 GiB), dense weights in anonymous buffers\n     3. Split dense trunk to mobile GPU, keep expert GEMMs on CPU\n   - **Required Content for Each Approach:**\n     - What is resident\n     - What is read from flash per token\n     - What a major page fault means here\n     - Why activating k=6 experts out of a large pool still leaves a large on-disk file\n   - **Concrete Decode Step Walkthrough:** Router scores, top-k, cache hit/miss, optional drop of cold low-weight expert, how it changes math and bytes\n   - **Closing Caveats:** (a) cache hit rate ≠ quality metric, (b) tok/s excluding prefill/draft ≠ user-perceived rate\n   - **Constraints:** 400-600 words, no markdown fences, no invented benchmark numbers"
